abstract: "ZebraFET is a free, open-source desktop application for conducting, managing, and analyzing acute zebrafish (Danio rerio) embryo toxicity tests — the Fish Embryo Acute Toxicity (FET) test — following OECD Test Guideline 236. It covers the full experimental workflow in one interface: project setup and concentration planning, plate layout, daily well scoring, photo documentation, and water-quality logging. Analysis covers lethal endpoints (LC50 by logistic regression with bootstrap confidence intervals, a distribution-free trimmed Spearman-Karber LC50, the LC50 refitted at each daily timepoint, NOEC/LOEC with Holm-Bonferroni correction, and Cochran-Armitage trend tests) and sublethal ones (per-endpoint malformation testing with false-discovery-rate control, a sublethal NOEC/LOEC, and a teratogenic index), with odds ratios and Wilson confidence intervals throughout. Test validity is assessed against every OECD TG 236 Section 9 criterion the recorded data supports. Results export as CSV tables and as a formatted Word report. ZebraFET runs on Windows, macOS, and Linux, and is released under the GNU General Public License v3.0."
